.TH AVR\-GROUP\-LIST 1 "" "avr" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-group-list \- List the organization's groups by path.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr group list
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
List the organization's groups by path.
.PP
A group's path is the display names from the root group down, joined with /, such as Organization/Platform/CI; a parent is listed before its children. Pass a group's ID or path to --group when you create or list service tokens.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr group list
    avr group list --json group_id,path --jq '.[].path'
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    created_at, display_name, group_id, label, member_count, ownership,
    parent_id, path, soft_deleted_at, state, suspension_reason, updated_at
.fi
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR, \fB\-o\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-limit\fR \fIINTEGER RANGE\fR
Max groups to return. (default: 50)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-group (1),
.BR avr-group-create (1),
.BR avr-group-delete (1),
.BR avr-group-edit (1),
